WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:00.400
All right.

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:00.934
Now to

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:03.036
this surprising discovery

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:05.472
that is defying the laws of science.

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:06.573
Crowds are flocking

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:07.040
to the small

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.742
town of Gower, Missouri,

00:00:08.742 --> 00:00:10.877
to view a Catholic nun's body

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:12.879
that appears to show no signs of decay

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:15.448
despite being buried for four years.

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:17.984
The body of Sister Wilhemina Lancaster,

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:21.121
who died in 2019 at the age of 95,

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:22.222
was exhumed

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:23.823
from the monastery grounds

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:25.258
so that she could be moved to her

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:27.761
final resting place inside the chapel.

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:30.363
But when her coffin was unearthed,

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.632
this is what they found.

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:33.833
Lancaster's body

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:35.368
was apparently incorrupt,

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:36.803
which in Catholic tradition

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:38.872
means the body did not decay.

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:42.042
CNN affiliate KMBC reports

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:43.143
people have traveled

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:44.844
from across the country

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:47.280
to see for themselves

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:49.649
Powerful

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:51.484
experience, very powerful.

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:53.353
It's one of the most rare events

00:00:53.353 --> 00:00:55.388
in the whole United States.

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:56.122
Not that old,

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:57.891
but I've never heard of that in my life.

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:01.628
Well, let me bring in Kelsey Wilkes.

00:01:01.795 --> 00:01:03.329
She is the executive director

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:04.597
for the HCI group

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:06.332
and has written about this

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:08.234
for the Catholic News Agency.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.203
Kelsey, good to see you.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:11.604
Thank you for having me.

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:13.640
So walk us through exactly

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:14.841
what this group of

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:17.110
sisters found when they unearthed

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:19.946
the body.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.782
Well, it's really remarkable, Fredricka.

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.551
When I sat down with the ABC,

00:01:24.551 --> 00:01:25.418
she said, you know,

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.353
we began to exhume

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:28.555
the body of our founders

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:29.622
to move her into the chapel.

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:30.857
It's a longstanding custom

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:32.525
in Catholic religious orders

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:34.094
to have your founders, founders

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:36.362
or founders and your in your chapel

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:38.698
and as we were exhuming her,

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:40.600
there was a crack in the coffin.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.802
And so she took a flashlight look ten.

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:44.871
And she goes, I think I saw soot.

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:45.972
And she said she couldn't

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:46.873
have seen a foot

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:48.675
at this point in the game.

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:50.143
There should be a great deal

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:51.010
of decomposition.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:51.678
They were expecting

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:53.613
to find skeletal remains

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:56.683
and instead they found an intact body.

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:58.151
So she said to her sisters,

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:01.454
I found a site and they all cheered,

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:03.389
knowing, of course, what

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:04.357
this potentially means

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:06.159
in Catholic tradition.

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:08.962
And so you actually went as well, right?

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:11.231
You went to see for yourself

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:12.599
and you and a whole

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:15.001
lot of people can see for themselves

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:17.670
because she is out in the open.

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:20.406
And what did you experience?

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:21.641
I mean, it was remarkable,

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:22.876
the level of detail.

00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:24.344
Even the brand name of her sock

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:26.379
was still visible

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:27.614
the veil of her habit

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:28.948
was made of the same material

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:31.050
as the interior lining of the coffin,

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.118
and that had decayed

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:34.287
while the veil had not.

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:37.590
There was no smell of putrid or decay

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:38.992
or anything of this.

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:39.392
It was

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:40.960
it was just simply looked

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:43.696
as though she had been dead for a day.

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:45.298
It was really remarkable.

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:48.067
And so help people understand, you know,

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:50.703
in the terms of Catholicism,

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:52.005
what is incorruptible?

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:53.239
What does it mean?

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:55.341
Does she seem to demonstrate

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:56.709
everything that it embodies?

00:02:58.578 --> 00:02:59.345
There's there does

00:02:59.345 --> 00:02:59.779
need to be

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:01.681
a thorough investigation to make sure

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:02.882
that this is

00:03:03.149 --> 00:03:05.351
was a case of an incorruptible

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:08.121
But what it essentially means

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:09.088
is that there's there's

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:11.291
a lack of natural process of decay.

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:13.760
And that points to a theological reality,

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:17.430
which is that you know, at this at this

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.033
at the end of this life,

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:21.601
there is something more.

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:23.203
And so people who demonstrate

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:25.004
extraordinary levels of holiness

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:27.273
within Catholicism often found

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:29.108
to have these incorrupt bodies,

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:30.577
which suggests that there's

00:03:30.577 --> 00:03:31.978
some level of closeness

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:33.546
to the future resurrection

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:34.981
that they might have

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.015
Is there anything more

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:37.350
you can tell us about who

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.719
Sister Wilhemina Lancaster was?

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:43.122
Yeah, she was 95 when she died.

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:45.225
She lived 75 years

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:46.226
in religious life

00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:46.893
under the vows

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:48.628
of poverty, chastity and obedience,

00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:50.763
which is its own miracle.

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:52.465
And at the age of 70,

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:53.933
she founded this congregation

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:55.368
of Benedictine Sisters.

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:56.102
They're known for their

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:58.504
chart-topping Gregorian Chant albums,

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:01.741
but they've also now become known

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:03.810
for the body of this woman

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:05.678
in an unnatural state of decay.

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:08.414
And who is giving hope to Catholics

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:09.115
and non-Catholics

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:11.517
around the country that maybe God is

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:13.286
is active.

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:14.654
Wow. So.

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:17.690
So what comes next for Sister Wilhelmina?

00:04:17.724 --> 00:04:17.991
I mean,

00:04:17.991 --> 00:04:19.225
what will the process

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:20.293
look like to determine

00:04:20.293 --> 00:04:23.463
if she, in fact, is an incorruptible

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:24.697
Know what

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:26.766
what does it take to ultimately

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:27.800
be declared a saint?

00:04:29.269 --> 00:04:30.036
Well,

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:32.672
first, on the level of incorruptibility,

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:34.440
it doesn't necessarily demonstrate

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.675
the holiness of her life,

00:04:35.675 --> 00:04:37.577
although it could be a sign of it.

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:39.479
So in order for her to be canonized,

00:04:39.479 --> 00:04:40.980
she'll have to go through a process

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:41.614
that will begin

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:43.416
after the fifth year of her death,

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:44.117
that will go through

00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:45.685
all of her writings, her

00:04:45.685 --> 00:04:47.654
her virtues, her life

00:04:47.654 --> 00:04:49.522
to see if there's anything in there

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:52.091
that is contradictory to the Christian

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:53.326
Christian way.

00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:54.360
And then after that,

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:55.595
she'll need two miracles,

00:04:55.595 --> 00:04:57.163
one miracle for beatification

00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:59.232
and one miracle for canonization.

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:00.233
And this

00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:02.702
this miracle, if it if it is found to be

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:06.806
not as a result of any sort of fluke

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:07.206
of the way

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:07.507
in which

00:05:07.507 --> 00:05:08.408
she was buried,

00:05:08.408 --> 00:05:10.443
or that the conditions within the ground,

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:12.278
which it does not appear

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:13.112
to be,

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:14.714
would not count for either

00:05:14.714 --> 00:05:16.749
of those two miracles. Hmm.

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:18.451
And what do you know about how she

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:19.986
was prepared for burial?

00:05:21.187 --> 00:05:22.722
So the abbess told me, and

00:05:22.722 --> 00:05:23.756
it's been confirmed

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:24.357
by the person

00:05:24.357 --> 00:05:25.158
who signed her death

00:05:25.158 --> 00:05:27.460
certificate that she was not involved

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.495
and that she was laid in a simple coffin

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:31.464
and without a concrete sarcophagus

00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:32.165
around it

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:34.434
and placed into the ground in Siena,

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:36.302
did a series of interviews

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:38.204
with morticians around the country.

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:38.971
And many of them

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:40.073
expressed their shock

00:05:40.073 --> 00:05:41.441
at the fact that a body

00:05:41.441 --> 00:05:42.775
that was not involved

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:45.645
would be at this point of lack of decay.

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:47.013
It's rather remarkable,

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:48.181
according to those that study

00:05:48.181 --> 00:05:49.182
mortuary science.

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:50.383
Wow. Is remarkable.

00:05:50.383 --> 00:05:50.883
That's why

00:05:50.883 --> 00:05:52.418
so many people are flocking there

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:53.886
to see for themselves.

00:05:53.886 --> 00:05:55.221
And apparently

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:58.424
there is a process that she'll you know,

00:05:58.424 --> 00:06:00.393
the body will actually be

00:06:00.393 --> 00:06:02.395
going through this week. Right.

00:06:02.395 --> 00:06:03.863
I mean, there'll be

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:06.799
a rosary involving her sisters and what

00:06:06.799 --> 00:06:07.433
else do you know?

00:06:08.568 --> 00:06:09.435
So there

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:10.570
what's fascinating is

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:12.805
there will be 20,000 visitors

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:14.073
by the end of this weekend.

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:15.074
They are anticipating.

00:06:15.074 --> 00:06:17.610
So they've had to set up a whole meet

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:18.644
and greet system.

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:19.579
They have porta potties

00:06:19.579 --> 00:06:21.080
down on the property.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:22.648
There are people in lines,

00:06:22.648 --> 00:06:23.282
the volunteers

00:06:23.282 --> 00:06:23.983
feeding them

00:06:23.983 --> 00:06:25.551
just to be able to walk through

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:26.853
and catch a glimpse of

00:06:26.853 --> 00:06:27.820
of sister's body

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.522
and to pray in front of it.

00:06:29.522 --> 00:06:31.457
And on the 29th

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:33.359
the sisters will hold a rosary procession

00:06:33.359 --> 00:06:35.995
and then they will formally move her body

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:36.729
into a glass

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:38.297
enclosed, enclosed case

00:06:38.297 --> 00:06:40.500
and put her final remains

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:42.168
inside the chapel with the sisters

00:06:42.168 --> 00:06:42.769
while they wait

00:06:42.769 --> 00:06:44.837
to build a shrine to Saint Joseph

00:06:44.837 --> 00:06:46.239
where they hope to bury her.

00:06:46.239 --> 00:06:47.373
Wow, that's incredible.

00:06:47.373 --> 00:06:48.541
And then potentially other

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:50.676
things could happen within the next year

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:51.744
because you mentioned the whole,

00:06:51.744 --> 00:06:55.047
you know, fifth year after one's death,

00:06:55.748 --> 00:06:58.050
potentially the process of canonization,

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:58.951
if it comes to that.

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:00.787
So wow, what a journey.

